Cell["\<\
Recast as a game: a referee sends independent random bits x to Alice and y to \
Bob; each answers a bit without communicating; they win if their answers a, b \
satisfy a\[CirclePlus]b = x\[And]y, the AND of the questions. Every classical \
strategy \[LongDash] deterministic or using shared randomness \[LongDash] \
wins at most 3/4 of the time. Sharing an entangled pair instead lets Alice \
and Bob win with probability cos^2(\[Pi]/8) = (2+\[Sqrt]2)/4 \[TildeTilde] \
0.854 \[LongDash] a real, provable, experimentally confirmed edge with no \
classical explanation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"edf7ec29-30b8-224c-9b7b-a524a0eb9a92"],

Cell["Classical bound, quantum value, and the gap between them:", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"fedd3d4f-8604-d94e-a746-b760ce2f13ef"],

Cell["{3/4, FullSimplify[Cos[Pi/8]^2], N[Cos[Pi/8]^2 - 3/4, 4]}", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3ca90409-1f2f-1a4f-97c0-dff2defbd985"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["3", "4"], ",", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
     FractionBox["\[Pi]", "8"], "]"}], "2"], ",", 
   "0.1035533905932737621`4."}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"72328ac5-\
e6f6-b349-ac1c-d6afb9eea2ef"],

Cell["\<\
The resource behind both numbers is entanglement: Alice and Bob share a \
single quantum state, like the Bell pair (|00\[RightAngleBracket]+|11\
\[RightAngleBracket])/\[Sqrt]2 used above, that cannot be split into \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]system A in some state\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]system B in some state\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
separately. Measuring one half instantaneously fixes the statistics of \
measuring the other, in a way no classical joint distribution over \
predetermined outcomes can reproduce \[LongDash] yet without letting either \
party send the other an actual signal: no measurement Alice performs changes \
Bob's own local statistics, so nothing here permits faster-than-light \
communication.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4832f807-4f73-a14b-b944-9654873f1757"],

Cell["\<\
CHSH needs two things at once: entanglement, and spatial separation \
\[LongDash] the two parties must be far enough apart that \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]no signaling\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] has real physical \
teeth. A natural question follows: is separation actually essential, or is \
entanglement doing all the work alone? Kochen and Specker (1967), and later \
Klyachko, Can, Binicioglu and Shumovsky (2008), showed the answer is no. A \
SINGLE quantum system \[LongDash] no entanglement, no separated parties, \
nothing but one qutrit and a sequence of measurements made on it \[LongDash] \
already forces the same kind of conclusion: no assignment of pre-existing \
values to measurement outcomes can reproduce quantum predictions, PROVIDED \
those values are required not to depend on which OTHER, compatible \
measurement happens to accompany them. This weaker, more general requirement \
\[LongDash] that an outcome shouldn't depend on its context, the other \
compatible measurements grouped with it \[LongDash] is called \
noncontextuality; its failure, contextuality, is strictly more general than \
nonlocality, of which Bell/CHSH is only the special spatially-separated case. \
The KCBS pentagon below is the smallest, sharpest example.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a1ee2148-7e62-004a-a344-e9757003dd1a"],

Cell["The Atom: The KCBS Pentagon", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"109e2847-7d0a-874c-a3fb-c41ce1841802"],

Cell["\<\
The five-cycle exclusivity graph C5 \[LongDash] five measurement outcomes, \
each excluding its two neighbors \[LongDash] is the smallest object carrying \
the full classical / quantum / post-quantum hierarchy identified by Cabello, \
Severini and Winter: the independence number \[Alpha](C5) = 2 bounds any \
noncontextual hidden-variable model, the Lov\[AAcute]sz number \
\[CurlyTheta](C5) = \[Sqrt]5 \[LongDash] Lov\[AAcute]sz's own 1979 pentagon \
example, the result that introduced this graph invariant in the first place \
\[LongDash] bounds quantum mechanics, and the fractional packing number \
\[Alpha]*(C5) = 5/2 bounds any no-signalling (post-quantum) theory. Because 2 \
< \[Sqrt]5 < 5/2 strictly, this one pentagon already separates all three \
levels. Everything below is built by composing copies of this atom.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"97012dcd-e03d-4f4d-b2b8-48795861e534"],

Cell["Build the C5 exclusivity graph:", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"0cc235b1-a6ce-8549-9081-80d98e04dada"],

Cell["\<\
Graph[CycleGraph[5], VertexStyle -> RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85], VertexSize -> \
0.4, EdgeStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.45], Thickness[0.01]], VertexLabels \
-> None, GraphLayout -> \"CircularEmbedding\", ImageSize -> 240, PlotLabel -> \
\"KCBS pentagon: the C5 exclusivity graph\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8fcb41eb-1197-d64b-9923-0115bb7af4b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  NamespaceBox["NetworkGraphics",
   DynamicModuleBox[{Typeset`graph = HoldComplete[
     Graph[{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, {Null, 
       SparseArray[
       Automatic, {5, 5}, 0, {
        1, {{0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}, {{2}, {5}, {1}, {3}, {2}, {4}, {3}, {5}, {
          1}, {4}}}, Pattern}]}, {EdgeStyle -> {
         Directive[
          GrayLevel[0.45], 
          Thickness[0.01]]}, 
       GraphLayout -> {
        "Dimension" -> 2, "VertexLayout" -> "CircularEmbedding"}, ImageSize -> 
       240, PlotLabel -> "KCBS pentagon: the C5 exclusivity graph", 
       VertexLabels -> {None}, VertexSize -> {0.4}, VertexStyle -> {
         RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]}}]]}, 
    TagBox[GraphicsGroupBox[{
       {GrayLevel[0.45], Thickness[0.01], Opacity[0.7], CapForm["Round"], 
        LineBox[{{
          DynamicLocation["VertexID$1", Automatic, Center], DynamicLocation[
           "VertexID$2", Automatic, Center]}, {
          DynamicLocation["VertexID$1", Automatic, Center], DynamicLocation[
           "VertexID$5", Automatic, Center]}, {
          DynamicLocation["VertexID$2", Automatic, Center], DynamicLocation[
           "VertexID$3", Automatic, Center]}, {
          DynamicLocation["VertexID$3", Automatic, Center], DynamicLocation[
           "VertexID$4", Automatic, Center]}, {
          DynamicLocation["VertexID$4", Automatic, Center], DynamicLocation[
           "VertexID$5", Automatic, Center]}}]}, 
       {RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85], EdgeForm[{GrayLevel[0], Opacity[0.7]}], 
        TagBox[
         DiskBox[{-0.9510565162951538, 0.3090169943749484}, 
          0.2351141009169891],
         "DynamicName",
         BoxID -> "VertexID$1"], 
        TagBox[DiskBox[{-7.044813998280222*^-16, 1.}, 0.2351141009169891],
         "DynamicName",
         BoxID -> "VertexID$2"], 
        TagBox[
         DiskBox[{0.9510565162951533, 0.30901699437494634`}, 
          0.2351141009169891],
         "DynamicName",
         BoxID -> "VertexID$3"], 
        TagBox[
         DiskBox[{0.5877852522924738, -0.8090169943749481}, 
          0.2351141009169891],
         "DynamicName",
         BoxID -> "VertexID$4"], 
        TagBox[
         DiskBox[{-0.5877852522924726, -0.8090169943749468}, 
          0.2351141009169891],
         "DynamicName",
         BoxID -> "VertexID$5"]}}],
     MouseAppearanceTag["NetworkGraphics"]],
    AllowKernelInitialization->False]],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"NetworkGraphics",
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,
  FrameTicks->None,
  ImageSize->240,
  PlotLabel->FormBox[
   "\"KCBS pentagon: the C5 exclusivity graph\"", TraditionalForm]]], "Output",\
ExpressionUUID->"bbc9cea8-9e93-6d4d-9110-edc9201ce1b8"],

Cell["\<\
The three numbers are three readings of the same five events. Classical: \
assign each event a definite 0 or 1 in advance; exclusivity forbids two \
adjacent 1s, so at most two events fire \[LongDash] \[Alpha](C5) = 2. \
Quantum: assign each event the probability cos^2 of an actual measurement \
direction against an actual state; the pentagon geometry below lets every \
event carry 1/\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] 0.447 simultaneously \[LongDash] summing \
to \[CurlyTheta](C5) = \[Sqrt]5. Exclusivity-only: forget mechanics entirely \
and demand only that adjacent events never both fire; probability 1/2 \
everywhere is then legal \[LongDash] \[Alpha]*(C5) = 5/2. One pentagon, three \
ceilings:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9942a67-109c-ba49-9c9f-e495b4c5ca9a"],

Cell["\<\
Read the same pentagon three ways \[LongDash] best classical assignment, \
quantum weights, bare-exclusivity halves:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"2e2871c6-7433-ba4e-b6fa-4983abab11c5"],

Cell["\<\
Module[{pts, pent, blue, amber}, blue = RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]; amber = \
RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.2]; pts = Table[{Cos[Pi/2 + 2*Pi*(q/5)], Sin[Pi/2 + \
2*Pi*(q/5)]}, {q, 0, 4}]; pent = Function[{vals, cols, sVal, title, sub}, \
Labeled[Graphics[{{GrayLevel[0.65], Thickness[0.006], Line[Append[pts, \
First[pts]]]}, Table[{cols[[q]], EdgeForm[GrayLevel[0.35]], Disk[pts[[q]], \
0.2], If[MatchQ[cols[[q]], GrayLevel[_]], Black, White], \
Text[Style[vals[[q]], 10, Bold], pts[[q]]]}, {q, 1, 5}]}, ImageSize -> 190, \
PlotRange -> 1.45, PlotRangePadding -> 0.12], Column[{Style[title, Bold, 10], \
Style[sub, Italic, 8, GrayLevel[0.45]], Style[StringJoin[\"\[CapitalSigma]p = \
\", sVal], 13, Bold]}, Alignment -> Center, Spacings -> 0.25], Top]]; \
Row[{pent[{\"1\", \"0\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0\"}, {blue, GrayLevel[0.82], blue, \
GrayLevel[0.82], GrayLevel[0.82]}, \"2\", \"CLASSICAL\", \"best 0/1 \
assignment: \[Alpha](C5)\"], pent[{\".45\", \".45\", \".45\", \".45\", \
\".45\"}, ConstantArray[blue, 5], \"\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeEqual] 2.236\", \"QUANTUM\
\", \"cos^2 weights: \[CurlyTheta](C5)\"], pent[{\"1/2\", \"1/2\", \"1/2\", \
\"1/2\", \"1/2\"}, ConstantArray[amber, 5], \"5/2\", \"EXCLUSIVITY ONLY\", \
\"no-signalling ceiling: \[Alpha]*(C5)\"]}, Spacer[8]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"76ad9908-5616-ed4e-be19-a5c09c185ef1"],

