     "0.44721359549995793928183473374625524709`15.163858242927772", ",", 
     "0.44721359549995793928183473374625524709`15.163858242927772", ",", 
     "0.44721359549995793928183473374625524709`14.825478516232122"}], "}"}], ",",
    "2.23606797749978969640917366873127623544`15.05302955554459", ",", 
   "2.23606797749978969640917366873127623544`20."}], "}"}]], "Output",Expressi\
onUUID->"7042da60-3cfb-7940-8eba-e7617f343ec1"],

Cell["\<\
The full KCBS inequality now follows from the same pipeline. Each event \
becomes a dichotomic observable A_k = 1 - 2|v_k\[RightAngleBracket]\
\[LeftAngleBracket]v_k|; adjacent pairs commute (their directions are \
orthogonal), so each product A_k A_(k+1) is itself a single \
jointly-measurable observable \[LongDash] one measurement context per \
pentagon edge. Any noncontextual assignment of pre-existing \[PlusMinus]1 \
values obeys \[CapitalSigma] \[GreaterEqual] -3; the qutrit's five contexts \
each return \[LeftAngleBracket]A_k A_(k+1)\[RightAngleBracket] = 1 - \
4/\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] -0.789, summing to 5 - 4\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] \
-3.944. This negative correlation form is the one experiments report \
\[LongDash] but it is the essay's positive event form in disguise: adjacent \
projector products vanish identically, so \
\[CapitalSigma]\[LeftAngleBracket]A_k A_(k+1)\[RightAngleBracket] = 5 - 4\
\[CenterDot]\[CapitalSigma]p EXACTLY, an affine change of ruler and nothing \
more. The last entry below converts the measured correlation sum back onto \
the event ruler and lands on \[Sqrt]5 \[LongDash] the same number the five \
projector probabilities summed to above:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0efcb508-6569-0249-824c-056780a96b68"],

Cell["\<\
Measure the five contexts \[LongDash] the commuting products A_k A_(k+1) \
\[LongDash] through QuantumMeasurementOperator, sum them against the \
noncontextual bound -3, and convert back to the event ruler:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"f477242e-a961-a94d-a0a8-92f1164a0ada"],

Cell["\<\
Module[{c2, vecs, projs, obs, handle, prod, corr}, c2 = Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + \
Cos[Pi/5]); vecs = N[Table[{Sqrt[1 - c2]*Cos[4*Pi*(i/5)], Sqrt[1 - \
c2]*Sin[4*Pi*(i/5)], Sqrt[c2]}, {i, 0, 4}], 20]; projs = (Outer[Times, #1, \
#1] & ) /@ vecs; obs = (IdentityMatrix[3] - 2*#1 & ) /@ projs; handle = \
QuantumState[{0, 0, 1}, 3]; prod[k_] := Module[{m = obs[[k]] . obs[[Mod[k, 5] \
+ 1]]}, (m + ConjugateTranspose[m])/2]; corr = \
Table[QuantumMeasurementOperator[prod[k]][handle][\"Mean\"], {k, 5}]; {corr, \
Total[corr], N[5 - 4*Sqrt[5], 20], -3, (5 - Total[corr])/4}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"75a5161a-f282-ac48-9acf-effb08608058"],

