Cell["Searching for the Optimal Word: ddt", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"63c5ecea-0060-db41-b30e-3218aebc0c2a"],

Cell["\<\
Neither pure orientation turns out to be optimal. Treating the ring as built \
from an infinite repeating word over the alphabet {d, t} \[LongDash] one \
letter per gluing joint \[LongDash] and searching over words rather than only \
the two pure orientations, the word (ddt)\[Infinity] (two direct joints, one \
twisted, repeated) was found to keep more quantum advantage per pentagon than \
pure twisted, by about 61%: gap(ddt) = 0.0698975\[Ellipsis] against \
gap(twisted) = \[Tau]* \[Minus] 4/3 \[TildeTilde] 0.043384. A slice of the \
mesh this word builds, glued into a closed ring \[LongDash] each block's own \
drawn orientation below is the real cumulative R_direct/R_twisted parity, not \
a schematic stand-in:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9f1b22a-ce09-4c4b-9b93-0e3bec40165c"],

Cell["\<\
Build the 51-pentagon ddt necklace; a block is drawn mirrored exactly when an \
odd number of twisted joints precede it:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"b54dc7f7-cc76-1240-99c1-d7552524b027"],

Cell["\<\
Module[{letters, np, rad, cumTwistedCount, mirrorQ, localPenta, centers, \
pentagons, joints, coral, cDirect, cTwisted}, letters = \
Characters[StringRepeat[\"ddt\", 17]]; np = Length[letters]; rad = \
0.62*(np/(2*Pi)); cumTwistedCount = FoldList[Plus, 0, (Boole[#1 === \"t\"] & \
) /@ letters][[1 ;; np]]; mirrorQ[k_] := OddQ[cumTwistedCount[[k + 1]]]; \
localPenta[mirror_] := Table[{Cos[2*Pi*(j/5) + Pi/2], If[mirror, -1, \
1]*Sin[2*Pi*(j/5) + Pi/2]}, {j, 0, 4}]; centers = \
Table[rad*{Cos[2*Pi*(k/np)], Sin[2*Pi*(k/np)]}, {k, 0, np - 1}]; pentagons = \
Table[(centers[[k + 1]] + 0.4*RotationTransform[2*Pi*(k/np)][#1] & ) /@ \
localPenta[mirrorQ[k]], {k, 0, np - 1}]; joints = Table[Module[{a = \
pentagons[[k + 1]], b = pentagons[[Mod[k + 1, np] + 1]], ja, jb}, ja = \
First[SortBy[a, EuclideanDistance[#1, Mean[b]] & ]]; jb = First[SortBy[b, \
EuclideanDistance[#1, Mean[a]] & ]]; {ja, jb}], {k, 0, np - 1}]; coral = \
RGBColor[0.9, 0.42, 0.15]; cDirect = RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]; cTwisted = \
RGBColor[0.06, 0.43, 0.46]; Graphics[{Table[{If[letters[[k + 1]] == \"d\", \
cDirect, cTwisted], Opacity[If[letters[[k + 1]] == \"d\", 0.8, 0.55]], \
EdgeForm[GrayLevel[0.3]], Polygon[pentagons[[k + 1]]]}, {k, 0, np - 1}], \
{coral, Opacity[0.85], Thickness[0.0035], Dashed, Line /@ joints}, {coral, \
PointSize[0.0035], Point[Flatten[joints, 1]]}}, ImageSize -> 640, PlotRange \
-> All, AspectRatio -> Automatic, PlotLabel -> \"a ddt necklace at scale: 51 \
pentagon blocks glued into a closed ring (153 detectors, 204 exclusivities); \
teal blocks mark an odd cumulative twisted-count -- a genuine reflection, not \
a decorative rotation\"]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c00741b2-f896-f049-84a6-f6a135ab5711"],

